hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15666","Hasan, meaning al-Ashyab, and Abu al-Nadr said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Abdullah ibn Qushayr, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, he said: Abu al-Nadr said in his hadith: Zuhayr narrated to us, Urwah ibn Abdullah ibn Qushayr Abu Mahal al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to me, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among a group of Muzaynah, and we pledged him, while his shirt was unbuttoned. He said: So we pledged him, then I put my hand in the pocket of his shirt and touched the seal. Then Urwah said: I never saw Muawiyah nor his son, Hasan meaning Abu Iyas, in winter ever nor in heat except with their garments unbuttoned, never buttoning them ever."
"15667","Rawh narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Qurrah narrating from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and sought his permission to put my hand in his garment opening, while he was supplicating for me, and nothing prevented him from my touching that he supplicated for me. He said: So I found on the cartilage of his shoulder like a lump. He narrated to us, he Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, and it is from the completion of the hadith of Qurrah, not that he is another Companion."
